Z||000001||batboy||10-29-2000||11:29 PM||||I have the RCC bump steer correction kit on my Batmobile. I have a couple pics somewhere, I'll look for them in a while. Here, in the mean time, I'll try to give you an idea what it looks like in this diagram.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/diagram.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-29-2000||11:44 PM||||The new RCC bump steer kit on the right and RCC rear coil-overs on the left.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/coilover.jpg"> <P>What it looks like installed. It completely replaces the old tie rod set-up.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/rearsuspension.jpg"> <BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||10-30-2000||06:53 AM||||excellent!  i kinda thought it had something to do with the tie rod's.  Bob Englert, and I had talked about it on saturday and decided that it somehow changed the pivit point of the tie rod... moving it out a little.<P>but i can tell im wrong.  <P>that looks nice.  how does it feel, compared to a car without it?<P>thanks! <P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
