Z||000008||bHooper||10-30-2000||11:22 AM||||Here is a reply that I just received from RCC about the bump steer kit:<P>"The function of the bump steer kit is to move the inboard pivot point of the<BR>drag link outboard several inches.  The kit includes two steel blocks that<BR>bolt to the inboard pivot point with a clevis on one end which the shortened<BR>drag link fastens to with the aid of a spherical bearing.  The stock outer<BR>tie rod end is used."<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||10-30-2000||04:56 PM||||I did all of the rear suspension rebuild at the same time, including the bump steer kit, so I don't know how much improvement was due to replacing worn out stock suspension parts plus the addition of the rear coil-over conversion kit or how much of it was due to the bump steer kit. Regardless, I was quite pleased with the end results. It handles very well now for having a big hunk of V8 sitting in the back.||||reg||1
